# partialscope — a source that could not be read reaches the answer: stated in
# the report body, or refused when the answer's medium cannot carry the
# statement. Never only a log line.
#
# The surface is derived by internal/surfaceaudit.PartialScopeSurface from the
# code that produces partial answers, not from a list of commands: every
# internal/cmd function returning a scope type (dashboardScanScope, sweepScope),
# and every companion route whose response declares a `Skipped` field. A site is
# any internal/cmd function that calls one of those. See dev/surfaces/README.md.
#
# D-7 has now been stated over the wrong set twice. The first version said "a
# dashboard", and the fix for a silent dashboard left a silent entity registry
# one function below it. The second said "a source of ref validate", and left
# `ref scan` returning three of twenty-four references at exit 0 with the whole
# config half dropped at slog.Warn — the same walk, the same channel, a command
# the rule's own prose named as deliberately exempt. This file is the set.
#
# The producers are exempt BY SHAPE, not by judgement: a function that returns
# the scope has handed the question to its caller, and every caller is a site.
# The exemption stops being true the day one of them starts printing.
#ceiling 0

internal/cmd/dash.go:scanDashboards = exempt: returns the scope to its caller and prints nothing; it is the producer, so the question it answers is asked at every call site instead
internal/cmd/ref.go:collectDashboardEntityRefs = exempt: returns the scope to its caller and prints nothing; ref validate decides what to do with it
internal/cmd/ref.go:planDashboardReplacements = exempt: returns the scope to its caller and prints nothing; ref replace refuses on it before any write

internal/cmd/dash.go:runDashGrep = proven: TestRunDashGrep_PartialIsStatedAndRefusesUnderJSON
internal/cmd/ref.go:runRefScan = proven: TestRunRefScan_PartialRefusesUnderJSONUnlessAllowPartial
internal/cmd/ref.go:runRefValidate = proven: TestRunRefValidate_SkippedConfigFilesTakeTheGate
internal/cmd/ref.go:refReplaceWithOptions = proven: TestRefReplaceRefusesWhenTheCompanionSkippedAFile
internal/cmd/ent.go:countRenameReferences = proven: TestEntRenameRefusesWhenTheConfigHalfSkippedAFile
internal/cmd/ent.go:runEntRename = proven: TestEntRenameRefusesWhenTheConfigHalfSkippedAFile
